WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.569 --> 00:00:11.480
Many of you have written us asking for a video
about what is going on in Turkey.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.480
And believe me, the

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:13.730
situation is quite dangerous.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.340
And… in case you were wondering…

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.480
NO, this time, Donald Trump is not to

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:18.480
blame for this.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.711
In fact, the US sanctions are just the tip
of the iceberg.

00:00:20.711 --> 00:00:23.090
An iceberg that could wreck

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.170
many many ships.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:27.230
And yes, the ships in this case, are the European
banks.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:32.940
Just look at this map.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.090
Turkey is a bridge between Europe and Asia.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:36.300
We’re talking about a country with a

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.510
population as big as Germany’s.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:42.800
A country where Europe has been investing
for decades: companies,

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.010
factories and, of course, lots and lots of
loans.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:47.160
Want an example?

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.160
Here you go.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:49.160
Have you ever heard of

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:50.160
the BBVA?

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.850
It’s the second biggest bank in Spain.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:54.930
Well, Turkey is the third biggest market for
this bank.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:55.930
In other words…

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:59.910
when the Turks sneeze a lot of Europeans end
up with a cold.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:01.500
Aren’t scared enough yet?

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.850
Well, listen up…

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:08.660
“Turkey is one of the most important NATO
members.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.890
After America, they have the biggest army
in the

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:11.890
alliance.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:15.390
And they are one of the few countries with
a Muslim majority and a secular constitution.

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:16.390
At

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:17.390
least…

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:18.390
so far.“

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:19.390
Yes, you heard this right.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:20.830
We said ‘so far’.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.820
The truth is, the Turkish president, RECEPT
TAYIPP ERDOGAN…

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:27.530
well, that man, he is not a big fan of secularism.

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:31.070
Erdogan is something like the ANAKIN SKYWALKER
of politics.

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.030
He started out as the good guy in the movie

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:40.000
but… we all know that, eventually, he will
fall to the dark side…

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.869
In this case, the dark side is a mix

00:01:44.869 --> 00:01:49.260
between religious fanaticism and good old
populism.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:52.810
Erdogan likes to portray himself as the defender
of the average man.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:54.730
Those turks that live in rural areas

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:58.170
like KONYA, completely outside of the glamour
of ISTANBUL.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.409
The turks there don’t have amazing salaries

00:02:00.409 --> 00:02:02.360
and they maintain a traditional lifestyle.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:05.390
And… who do they need to be protected against?

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:06.490
Well, of

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:10.649
course, the Western conspiracy that wants
to end Turkey!

00:02:10.649 --> 00:02:17.530
This explains why news like this is so important
for Erdogan’s narrative.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:23.540
U.S. Imposes Sanctions on Turkish Officials
Over Detained American Pastor

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:26.860
Nonetheless, this is just the tip of the iceberg.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:29.959
First of all, the actual reason behind the
US sanctions

00:02:29.959 --> 00:02:34.989
is not the pastor but the military and situations
with the Kurds in Syria.

00:02:34.989 --> 00:02:36.570
But that’s another story for

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.570
another video.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:41.070
The truth is Turkey’s crisis has been going
on for three years already.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:42.070
And this isn’t

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:43.190
just a political crisis!

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:45.600
In fact, the biggest problem is economics.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.359
We’re talking about a small scale

00:02:47.359 --> 00:02:48.389
Venezuela…

00:02:48.389 --> 00:02:51.199
at the very gates of Europe.

00:02:51.199 --> 00:02:54.140
But now the question is… what is going on
in Turkey?

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:57.030
What happened in this country to cause them
to fall

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.770
to the dark side of economics?

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:01.480
Do we really have reasons to be scared?

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:02.761
Today we are going to answer all

00:03:02.761 --> 00:03:10.200
of these questions but before we do, let’s
take a look back at history.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.310
ERDOGAN, THE SAVIOUR

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:21.160
Turkey is famous for many things: Saint Sophia,
kebabs and… inflation!

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:23.400
Since 1970, and until the year

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:26.140
2000, Turkey had sky high inflation rates.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:29.070
Many years they even surpassed the 100% mark.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:30.070
This means that,

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:33.250
from one year to the next, prices would double.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:37.970
And what happens when you have so much inflation
and you live so close to wealthy European

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:38.970
countries?

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:47.840
Well… you become a cheap labor Disneyland!

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:51.400
Companies like RENAULT of PEUGEOT built lots
of factories in

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:52.400
Turkey.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:55.299
And I know what you’re gonna say now…

00:03:55.299 --> 00:03:59.960
‘OK, Simon, but this is good news for a
country, isn’t

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:00.960
it?’.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:02.690
Well, yes… and at the same time, no.

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:07.509
For example, in the 60s, Renault opened a
factory in BURSA, a city in northern Turkey.

00:04:07.509 --> 00:04:08.509
Manufacturing cars

00:04:08.509 --> 00:04:10.510
in Bursa was very cheap for Renault.

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:13.720
Since the Turkish lira was devaluating year
after year, Renault had

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:16.500
to pay lower salaries.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:24.490
Nonetheless, once they got the money from
selling those cars…

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:25.490
Do you think they

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:27.190
kept that wealth inside of the country?

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:28.190
Of course not!

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:30.170
If Turkish money was losing value so fast,
the

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:35.730
smartest thing you could do was take the money
out ASAP.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:39.880
This is why Turkey seemed doomed to stagnation…

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.020
Until the year 2003.

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:43.380
That’s the year when Erdogan came to

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:49.230
power.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:52.900
His main goal was to keep inflation below
10%.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.110
He created a new currency, the New Turkish
Lira.

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:56.110
A

00:04:56.110 --> 00:05:05.380
currency far more stable than the previous
one.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:08.260
And as soon as inflation was at hand, the
Turkish economy

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:11.200
made a 180 degree shift.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.540
All of a sudden, many European companies started
investing in Turkey.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:15.980
This included banks.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:16.980
One of them,

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:21.320
the Spanish BBVA, invested on this country
big time.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.100
So much so that now Turkey is their third
largest

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:25.100
market.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:27.040
So in the 2000s, Turkey was in fashion.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:30.590
Rule of law and monetary stability meant that
companies could

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:32.130
reinvest in the country.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:36.830
So in less than 10 years, your average Turkish
worker went from making 800 USD a

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:43.760
month to making more than 1200 USD a month.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:48.810
But not only that!

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:52.770
In those first Erdogan years, new industries
like tourism developed.

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:53.770
Turkey went from

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.710
13 million tourists to 39 million.

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:57.930
And what about Turkish companies?

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:00.650
Well… have you ever heard of TURKISH AIRLINES?

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:01.650
In the 90s, Turkish

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:03.540
Airlines was just another airline carrier.

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:06.580
But since they could now reinvest their profit,
they ended up

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:08.910
becoming an aviation juggernaut.

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:12.930
And, believe me, they are not an isolated
case.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:17.740
If there’s one great example of the Turkish
Miracle, it’s YILDIZ HOLDINGS.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:18.950
This company started out as a

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:23.650
family owned bakery and now they’ve already
bought European brands like GODIVA CHOCOLATES

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:24.700
or UNITED

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:25.700
BISCUITS.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:31.170
Today, YILDIZ HOLDINGS is the World’s third
biggest company in the food sector.

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:32.170
So in other words…

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:40.520
the Turkish economy was ON FIRE.

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:42.250
And since the economy was ON FIRE, nobody
seemed to

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:45.740
care about the fact that Erdogan had spent
some time in prison for being part of a radical

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:46.740
Group.

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:47.740
At the

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:51.760
end of the day, the country was still democratic
and Erdogan was the arab rockstar.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.290
The chosen one to

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:55.970
bring the Islamic world to the… bright side.

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:58.960
Back then, Turkey wanted to be European.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:01.950
They were just about to become a member of
the European Union.

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:07.990
As a fun fact, in 2003 they won the Eurovision
song contest.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:13.000
But, you know, the negotiations to become
a

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:17.600
EU member extended over time… and What happened?

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:18.600
Well…

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:20.840
Erdogan lost his patience and he said…

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:21.840
Oh!

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:23.110
So am I not cool enough to join your club?

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:24.270
Well you know what?

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:26.580
I’m tired of being so Western, having

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:29.340
separation of powers, secularism and I-don’t-know-what-else.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:31.580
All of that is over.

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:34.230
Now is the time for…

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:38.950
THE NEW ERDOGAN-O-MICS

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:41.350
In the last 5 years, things started to sour
for Erdogan.

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:43.330
First, he was personally involved in many

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:44.360
corruption cases.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:48.669
But worst of all was news like this.

00:07:48.669 --> 00:07:55.980
Istanbul Ataturk airport attack: 41 dead and
more than 230 hurt

00:07:55.980 --> 00:08:00.290
DAESH attacks have brought Islamic terrorism
and insecurity to the streets of Turkey.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.290
And the damage to

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:02.610
the tourism industry was immediate.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:06.820
In just 2 years, tourism income has fallen
by 25%.

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:07.820
And this is

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:12.180
specially worrying given that tourism accounts
for 13% of the Turkish economy.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:13.389
But that’s not all…

00:08:13.389 --> 00:08:15.639
Foreign investment has fallen by half.

00:08:15.639 --> 00:08:17.740
And you might wonder…

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:18.740
why?

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:19.740
Well… there are two

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:20.750
reasons for this.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:24.040
The first one is the lack of a chance that
Turkey is going to become part of the

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:25.280
European Union.

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:27.139
The second is Erdogan itself.

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:32.130
Yes, my dear viewers, Islamic radicalism is
not just a danger politics wise.

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:34.229
It is also the worst for

00:08:34.229 --> 00:08:35.769
economics.

00:08:35.769 --> 00:08:44.039
Turkey's Erdogan calls interest rates "mother
of all evil"; lira slides

00:08:44.039 --> 00:08:49.060
According to Erdogan, the so-called ‘economic
orthodoxy’ is a Western invention that will

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:50.310
destabilize

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:51.310
Turkey.

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:53.240
This borrowing money with interest thing goes
against Islam.

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:55.060
So, he went to the Central Bank and

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:58.650
forced them to lower the interest rates and
start printing money.

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:01.780
And what if the Central Banker doesn’t

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:02.780
want to do that?

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:06.550
Well, these are Erdogan’s words.

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:12.620
"the central bank can't take this independence
and set aside the signals given by the president."

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:13.620
–

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:14.850
Erdogan speaking to Bloomberg

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:19.640
So, in other words, after the failed coup
d’etat of 2016, Erdogan has finally fallen

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:23.610
to the dark side.

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:27.080
He

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.930
thinks he can manage the economy at his will.

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:32.960
And every rational critic against his economic
policy will

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.790
be seen as a Western conspirator.

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:38.460
He even named his son in law as Finance Minister.

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:39.460
This new economic

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:42.900
paradigm is not a free market or social democracy…

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:45.540
this is the new Erdogan-o-mics.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:53.390
Do you need Money to pay for your spending?

00:09:53.390 --> 00:09:54.390
You print it!

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:55.560
Are Turkish companies complaining?

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:56.560
You flood

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:57.860
the market with cheap credit!

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:01.210
In less than 2 years, Turkish Banks have given
more than 50 billion dollars

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:02.270
worth of loans.

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:05.110
And all of this with almost no interest.

00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:06.110
The result?

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:08.950
A crazy devaluation of the Turkish Lira.

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:14.680
“In the year 2014, the American Dollar was
Exchanged by, more or less, 2.5 liras.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:17.000
By the time we make

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:21.170
this video, the exchange rate was more than
6 liras per 1 dollar.

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:22.649
This means that the Turkish lira has

00:10:22.649 --> 00:10:25.610
one third of the value it had before.

00:10:25.610 --> 00:10:32.290
And this explains why inflation rates rose
to 11.9% in 2017.“

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:33.779
OK, OK!

00:10:33.779 --> 00:10:37.520
I know what you’re thinking…

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:38.520
11.9%?

00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:41.149
That doesn’t sound so bad, right?

00:10:41.149 --> 00:10:42.149
In Argentina, for instance,

00:10:42.149 --> 00:10:43.600
they have 3 times more inflation.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:47.150
The truth is that you need some time between
a devaluation and the rise

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:48.640
in day to day prices.

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:51.470
So who are the first ones suffering from the
effects of this devaluation?

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:52.470
Well…

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:54.750
those would be the companies that had loans
in foreign banks.

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.230
And there are more than a few!

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:57.230
Do you

00:10:57.230 --> 00:10:58.230
remember YILDIZ HOLDINGS?

00:10:58.230 --> 00:10:59.580
That food industry behemoth?

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:04.420
Well, here you go…

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:09.470
Turkish owner of Godiva chocolate to restructure
$6.5 billion of debt

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:14.589
Estimations say that foreign debt from Turkish
companies surpasses 300 billion dollars.

00:11:14.589 --> 00:11:15.589
For a better

00:11:15.589 --> 00:11:19.080
understanding, this is the same amount of
money spent in all of the bailouts to Greece.

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:20.080
And meanwhile,

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:23.470
the inflation rate is starting to grow little
by little.

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:25.990
This year, 2018, it has already reached 15%.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:26.990
And

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:32.350
all the non-governmental estimations say that,
at the beginning of 2019, it will rise to

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:35.350
22%.

00:11:35.350 --> 00:11:42.110
Turkey Cut Deeper Into Junk as S&amp;P Sees Recession
Next Year

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:44.630
Add to this the sanctions imposed by Donald
Trump.

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:47.250
We will talk about the reasons behind the
sanctions in

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:48.370
another video.

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:50.110
Here we want to focus on the economics.

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:51.660
Because in the middle of all this, there is

00:11:51.660 --> 00:12:00.590
another player with a lot to lose: The European
Union.

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:05.680
Banks like the Spanish BBVA, the French BNP
Paribas or the Italian UNICREDIT have lent

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:07.140
more than 190

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:08.970
billion dollars to Turkish companies.

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:13.020
So far, BBVA has already lost half of the
value of those

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:14.020
investments.

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:18.170
So you can already imagine the big gap that
a Turkish collapse would leave.

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:22.190
So far, Erdogan has said he won’t ask for
a bailout from the International Monetary

00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:23.529
Fund and he will not

00:12:23.529 --> 00:12:25.440
raise capital controls either.

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:26.440
But…

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:28.399
can he stick to his words?

00:12:28.399 --> 00:12:29.500
We just don’t know.

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:30.589
All we know is that

00:12:30.589 --> 00:12:34.330
both Qatar and China have already promised
to help the Turkish economy.

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:36.340
But it is still too soon to see

00:12:36.340 --> 00:12:41.860
what will happen.

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:44.480
So now the question goes to all of you…

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:46.750
Will Turkey become the European Venezuela?

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:51.240
Can this crisis trigger a bigger crisis all
across Europe?

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:57.399
Could Erdogan pull everybody to the dark side?

00:12:57.399 --> 00:13:03.209
Please leave your answers in the comment section
below.

